<rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" version="2.0"><channel><title>textmate – justaddwater.dk</title><link>https://justaddwater.dk/tag/textmate/</link><description>Instant Usability &amp; Web Standards — static archive</description><language>en-US</language><atom:link href="https://justaddwater.dk/tag/textmate/feed/" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /><item><title>How To add “Open folder in Textmate” to Finder Context Menu</title><link>http://justaddwater.dk/2009/12/08/how-to-add-open-folder-in-textmate-to-finder-context-menu/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">http://justaddwater.dk/?p=1252</guid><dc:creator>Jesper Rønn-Jensen</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 08 Dec 2009 09:44:43 +0000</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;I wanted to add a menu item in Finder’s context menu that would open the selected folder in Textmate.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="/wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Screen-shot-2009-12-08-at-10.24.20-AM.png"&gt;&lt;img alt="Textmate context menu item: Open selected folder in  Textmate" class="aligncenter size-medium wp-image-1253" height="300" sizes="(max-width: 289px) 100vw, 289px" src="/wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Screen-shot-2009-12-08-at-10.24.20-AM-289x300.png" srcset="/wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Screen-shot-2009-12-08-at-10.24.20-AM-289x300.png 289w, /wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Screen-shot-2009-12-08-at-10.24.20-AM.png 366w" title="Textmate context menu item: Open selected folder in  Textmate" width="289"/&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A google search suggested the method described by K. Adam Christensen on his blog: “&lt;a href="http://shifteleven.com/articles/2006/09/17/opening-a-directory-in-textmate-from-finder"&gt;Opening a directory in TextMate from Finder&lt;/a&gt;“. However, from the documentation, I learned that that method is now outdated. Snow Leopard users should use “Services” and not “workflow” for setting this up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here is what I did:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Open Automator.app. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From the menu item “File” &amp;gt; “New” choose “Services”&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="/wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Screen-shot-2009-12-08-at-10.22.00-AM.png"&gt;&lt;img alt="Automator-File-New-Service" class="aligncenter size-medium wp-image-1254" height="280" sizes="(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" src="/wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Screen-shot-2009-12-08-at-10.22.00-AM-300x280.png" srcset="/wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Screen-shot-2009-12-08-at-10.22.00-AM-300x280.png 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Screen-shot-2009-12-08-at-10.22.00-AM.png 546w" title="Automator-File-New-Service" width="300"/&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Now there are 3 steps to be filled out like so:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="/wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Screen-shot-2009-12-08-at-10.23.23-AM.png"&gt;&lt;img alt='Automator final setup for "open in textmate" Finder.app context menu itm' class="aligncenter size-medium wp-image-1255" height="152" sizes="(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px" src="/wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Screen-shot-2009-12-08-at-10.23.23-AM-300x152.png" srcset="/wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Screen-shot-2009-12-08-at-10.23.23-AM-300x152.png 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2009/12/Screen-shot-2009-12-08-at-10.23.23-AM.png 881w" title='Automator final setup for "open in textmate" Finder.app context menu itm' width="300"/&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
First, edit the top so that “Service recieves selected: &lt;strong&gt;files or folders&lt;/strong&gt; in &lt;strong&gt;Finder.app&lt;/strong&gt;“.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Second, add the action “Get Selected Finder Items” from the left column (use the search field to find, then drag selected into the right work area).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Third, add the action “Run Shell Script” to your service. Fill in the following command:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;cat | xargs mate&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Finally, choose “File” &amp;gt; “Save…” and give it a name like “Open in Textmate”&lt;/p&gt;
</description></item></channel></rss>